Kalyan Jewellers India shares rose in early trade on Tuesday after UBS initiated coverage on the jewellery retailer with a ‘buy’ rating and a target price of Rs 900 per share, implying an upside of nearly 50 percent from Friday’s closing price. The Kalyan Jewellers stock was trading 1.5 percent higher at Rs 610 in early deals. The shares had closed 1.89 percent lower at Rs 601.15 on Friday. Indian stock markets were shut on Monday for a holiday.
UBS said Kalyan Jewellers has emerged as a pan-India jewellery retailer, replicating market leader Titan’s footprint while building a strong hyper-local value proposition. The brokerage highlighted the company’s capital-light franchise-owned, company-operated (FOCO) model, which is now well established and allows Kalyan Jewellers to expand its network aggressively. Its pace of store additions is nearly twice that of Titan, according to UBS.
